{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you today. Can you tell me what happened that brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I… I took a bunch of tramadol and Phenergan. I didn’t want to feel anything anymore. I was arguing with my mom, and I just couldn’t handle it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you for telling me. I’m sorry you’re going through this. You drove yourself here after, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah. I knew I needed help. I didn’t want to die, not really. I just wanted the pain to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You did the right thing coming in. In the ER, you had a brief episode where you weren’t breathing well and got a dose of Narcan. You responded quickly, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember waking up confused. Was I in danger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was brief and we caught it. No lasting effects. We’ve been monitoring you closely. Your labs are stable, and your breathing is normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been on tramadol for my endometriosis pain. But I know it’s not helping my mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re stopping tramadol now. It can affect your mental health, especially with your history. We’ll manage your pain another way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had bipolar disorder for years. I’ve had ECT before during pregnancy. It helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your records show that. Psychiatry has reviewed your case. They recommend restarting ECT, and we agree."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared. Last time I had a reaction to Haldol. I felt stiff and couldn’t move well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. You’re allergic to Haldol and a few others. We’ve flagged that. No one will give you those meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been sober since I got pregnant. I used to abuse opioids when I was a nurse. I don’t want to go back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been through a lot. But you’ve stayed clean, and that’s strong. We’ll make sure your treatment supports that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CT scan of your head when you arrived to make sure there was no brain injury. It came back normal—no bleeding or stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was confused at first. I thought maybe something was wrong up here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The confusion was likely from the overdose. It’s clearing now. Your repeat labs this morning are good—kidneys, liver, electrolytes all stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other meds? I take Seroquel, levothyroxine, ranitidine…"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re still on levothyroxine for your thyroid and ranitidine for reflux. Seroquel was adjusted—psychiatry lowered it to 150mg at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why lower it? Was it causing problems?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not causing harm, but with your mood instability, they want to balance effectiveness and side effects. You also now have a PRN dose for anxiety—25mg as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been using the lidocaine patch for pelvic pain. Can I keep that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s safe to continue. We’ll also keep your prenatal vitamins and Depo-Provera shot as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still hurt, but I don’t want to rely on opioids again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-06-18 10:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with your gynecologist on non-opioid options. For now, the patch and other supports should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. Slept okay. Still sad, but not as overwhelmed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. Your labs from this morning look even better—creatinine improved, electrolytes normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe for me to go to the psych unit for ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ve medically cleared you. No complications from the overdose. You’re stable for transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do I need to do before ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to be NPO—nothing to eat or drink—after midnight the night before your first treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Will I be able to go home after ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-06-19 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That will depend on how you respond. The team will reassess after a few sessions. For now, focus on getting treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day. You’re being discharged to the psychiatric unit for ECT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous, but ready. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You’ve made a brave choice. Your discharge meds are set: same as before, but tramadol is stopped, and Seroquel is 150mg nightly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I can use the PRN Seroquel if I’m anxious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, up to four times a day if needed. Keep using your inhaler for asthma, thyroid and reflux meds, and the lidocaine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will someone help me with my mom? She depends on me, but it’s hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The social worker will follow up. There may be support services to help ease the burden while you focus on recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would help. I don’t want to hurt myself again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you won’t have to. You’re getting the right care now. Keep reaching out when you’re struggling—it’s a strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-06-20 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and I hope to hear you’re doing well soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-06-18 09:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-06-20 18:25:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A patient with a history of refractory bipolar disorder, depression, and prior suicide attempts was admitted after a suicide attempt involving an intentional overdose of tramadol and Phenergan. She self-presented to the ED after an argument with her mother, whom she cares for. In the ED, she had a brief episode of hypoxia and reduced responsiveness, responded to Narcan, and was stabilized. She was monitored for 48 hours without complications. A CT head showed no acute abnormalities. Her psychiatric medications were adjusted, with quetiapine reduced to 150mg nightly and a PRN dose added for agitation. Tramadol was discontinued due to its risk in mood disorders and substance use history. She was medically cleared and discharged to an inpatient psychiatric facility for ECT. Chronic conditions including hypothyroidism and GERD were managed with continued levothyroxine and ranitidine. The patient expressed ongoing chronic pelvic pain from endometriosis but committed to avoiding opioid dependence. Social stressors related to caregiving were acknowledged, and support services were recommended.",
    "problems": [
      "Poisoning by other synthetic narcotics, intentional self-harm, initial encounter",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Poisoning by other antiepileptic and sedative-hypnotic drugs, intentional self-harm, initial encounter",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Opioid abuse, uncomplicated",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Endometriosis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
